{
    "npc_key": "lise_fenner",
    "start": "greeting",
    "nodes": {
        "greeting": [
            {
                "conditions": [
                    {
                        "quest": "the_fenmoor_lot",
                        "stage": "the_day_book"
                    }
                ],
                "text": "The hulk with the blue rail is the tidiest thing on the mud. A woman of about fifty is scrubbing a pot on the deck, and when you say Wat's name she stops, and dries her hands, and goes below without a word, and comes back up with a book bound in oilcloth.\n\n\"Twenty years,\" Lise Fenner says. \"Loads and tolls. I can't read it. I know it's his because it's his hand.\" She opens it on the rail where the light is. \"You'll want four winters back. People who come asking always want one particular page.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Read four winters back.",
                        "next": "the_page"
                    },
                    {
                        "label": "Leave.",
                        "end": true
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "conditions": [
                    {
                        "flag": "armour_chain_fate",
                        "equals": "paid"
                    }
                ],
                "text": "Lise Fenner nods to you from the deck of the blue-rail hulk. \"Jory crossed it out,\" she says. \"Drew a line through it in front of me. I've never seen him do that for anybody.\" She goes back to her pot.",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Leave.",
                        "end": true
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "text": "Lise Fenner is scrubbing the same pot, or another one. \"Did it help?\" she asks, and then, before you can answer: \"No. It never does. Go on.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Leave.",
                        "end": true
                    }
                ]
            }
        ],
        "the_page": [
            {
                "text": "The hand is big and careful and it does not change in twenty years.\n\n*Weir. 4 crates plate &c. off Darrow, 11 gp. East road.*\n\n*Fold. Salt, 2 sacks, Hobb's farm, as asked. Paid.*\n\n*Hill store. 1 crate left, as asked. Paid.*\n\n*Ford. Toll 3d.*\n\nThat is all. A carter's week. The crate that Nakka wore for four years is one line between a farmer's salt and a toll.",
                "interjections": [
                    {
                        "companion": "ilse",
                        "text": "Ilse: \"The hill store. That's the warren's dry store. He left it at their door, and he was paid, and he went on to the ford.\""
                    },
                    {
                        "companion": "kessa",
                        "text": "Kessa: \"Paid by who? It doesn't say by who.\""
                    }
                ],
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "'As asked.' Who asked him?",
                        "next": "as_asked"
                    },
                    {
                        "label": "Go through every 'as asked' in the book.",
                        "check": {
